      "side": 1,
      "message": "for now this looks right.  with sve/sme the 16 byte vectors may want to change, but they still use 16 bytes for sve and can dup the values.  sve has a 16 byte lane concept that i dont fully understand, since hardware really doesnt exist.\n\nA mistake we made for YuvConstants was to make 32 bit arm different than 64 bit.\nLast time I looked the 32 bit one made more sense.  Not a big deal.\n\nI had hoped RGB To YUV could use the same constants on all platforms, architecting it for 8 bit dot products.  But at the moment avx wants 32 elements vs neon wants 16.  Both could use scalar.. but here that would be 4 bytes for RGBToY\nNot a priority.. only the name needs to be the same.",
